/**
\fn pdg::getInterfaceMetadata(string interfaceName, string memberName)
\brief Return an independent structured description of the available interface.

With both arguments omitted, returns the module inventory, including classes,
constants, functions, inherited methods, overload parameter lists, defaults, return
contracts, and shared record and callback schemas. With interfaceName, returns
that class or root export. With both names, returns the selected member and all
its overloads. Use "pdg" as interfaceName to select a root member.

No constructors, methods, or property getters are invoked. Exports unavailable
in the current build are omitted. Every result is an independent copy; changing
it does not change subsequent queries. Accessor values are not evaluated.

\param interfaceName Optional interface or root export name.
\param memberName Optional member name within the selected interface.
\return A plain metadata record. Invalid selector types throw TypeError; unknown
names throw RangeError.

\code{.js}
const move = pdg.getInterfaceMetadata('Polygon', 'moveTo');
for (const params of move.params) {
    console.log(params.map(param => param.type + ' ' + param.name).join(', '));
}
console.log(pdg.describeInterface('Polygon', 'moveTo'));
\endcode

\sa pdg::describeInterface
*/

/**
\fn pdg::describeInterface(string interfaceName, string memberName)
\brief Format structured interface metadata as readable signatures.

Uses the same selectors, available interfaces, independent metadata, and errors
as getInterfaceMetadata(). Includes each overload, parameter defaults, return
type, and brief description. With a class or module selector, lists its members.

\param interfaceName Optional interface or root export name.
\param memberName Optional member name within the selected interface.
\return A string describing the selected interface or member.
\sa pdg::getInterfaceMetadata
*/
